<title>UK: UK notes in circulation rise 6.0 percent.</title>
<headline>UK notes in circulation rise 6.0 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>British bank notes in circulation rose an adjusted 6.0 percent in the week to April 30 compared with the equivalent week a year ago, the Bank of England said.</p>
<p>Last week the annual rise was 5.8 percent.</p>
<p>NOTES IN CIRCULATION (in rounded bln stg) -</p>
<p>				Latest week  pvs week	yr-ago week</p>
<p> Notes in circulation     21.35	   20.97	   20.15</p>
<p> Bankers' deposits	   2.096	   2.019	   1.91</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7715</p>
</text>
